─────────────────────────────────────────
COMIC MANAGEMENT
─────────────────────────────────────────

ComicManager  (MonoBehaviour — panel registry + loop/panel pointer ONLY)
  │     List<IComicPanel> Panels      (assigned in Inspector; sorted by rank at Start())
  │     IComicPanel CurrentPanel
  │     LoopCount CurrentLoop
  │     AdvancePanel()       ──►  PanelSelector.NextPanel → CommandHistory.Execute(new SwitchCameraCommand)
  │     RetreatPanel()       ──►  CommandHistory.Undo()
  │     RedoPanel()          ──►  CommandHistory.Redo()
  │     ReplayCurrentPanel() ──►  CurrentPanel.Replay()
  └── Does NOT own focus choices — delegates to PlayerChoicesSO

PanelSelector  (plain C# — pure static helper, no MonoBehaviour)
  │     static IComicPanel NextPanel(List<IComicPanel> panels, IComicPanel current, LoopCount loop)
  └── Eligibility rule: firstLoop <= currentLoop <= lastLoop
      All loop-eligibility logic lives here only — never duplicated elsewhere

CommandHistory  (plain C# — two-stack undo/redo)
  │     Stack<ICommand> _history      (panels visited so far)
  │     Stack<ICommand> _future       (panels available to go forward to after Undo)
  │     Execute(ICommand cmd)         (push to history, clear future, cmd.Execute())
  │     Undo()                        (pop history → push future → cmd.Undo())
  │     Redo()                        (pop future → push history → cmd.Redo())
  └── Named "History" not "Queue" — models undo/redo, not FIFO processing

─────────────────────────────────────────
NAVIGATION
─────────────────────────────────────────

NavigationController  (MonoBehaviour — owns Input, calls ComicManager)
  │     // Subscribe to InputAction.performed in OnEnable; unsubscribe in OnDisable (event-driven)
  │     // _inputBlocked = true on Advance; unblocked ONLY via OnPanelReadyForInput
  │     // No CinemachineBrain dependency — camera activation does NOT unblock input
  └── NavigationPresenter  (MonoBehaviour — UI display only, no logic)
        // Shows/hides back arrow, forward arrow, replay button, advance hint
        // Reads ComicManager state via events; never calls Advance/Retreat directly

─────────────────────────────────────────
COMIC PANEL
─────────────────────────────────────────

IComicPanel
  │     int Rank
  │     LoopCount FirstLoop
  │     LoopCount LastLoop
  │     CinemachineBlendDefinition IncomingBlend
  │     bool HasBeenVisited
  │     UnityEvent OnPanelComplete      (raised when all steps done and panel is ready to exit)
  │     UnityEvent OnReadyForInput      (raised when the advance button should be enabled)
  │     void Show()                     (entry animation — forward story progression only)
  │     void ShowInstant()              (end state, no animation — history navigation only)
  │     void Replay()                   (reset + Show() — called by Replay button)
  │     void Hide()
  │     void Advance()
  └── ComicPanel  (MonoBehaviour — implements IComicPanel)
        │     [SerializeField] PanelDataSO data          (designer sets rank, loop, variant flags)
        │     [SerializeField] PlayerChoicesSO choices   (read at Show()/ShowInstant() time)
        │     [SerializeField] CinemachineCamera cam     (child object; assigned in Inspector)
        │     [RequireComponent] Animator anim           (same GameObject; resolved via GetComponent in Awake)
        │     IPanelStep[] _steps                        (collected via GetComponentsInChildren in Awake)
        │
        │     Show()        ──►  enable cam+anim, deactivate all steps, play Intro, wait for completion
        │     ShowInstant() ──►  enable cam+anim, activate steps where ShowInFinalState=true, snap to end
        │     Hide()        ──►  disable cam+anim, stop coroutine
        │     Replay()      ──►  PrepareForReplay() all steps, reset HasBeenVisited, call Show()
        │     Advance()     ──►  activate next step; lock input if IsBlocking; fire OnPanelComplete when done
        │
        │     HasBeenVisited is set at the END of WaitForIntroCompletion() — not at the start of Show().
        │     (If set early, navigating away mid-animation leaves HasBeenVisited=true, causing the panel
        │      to skip to its end state on the next forward visit instead of replaying the animation.)
        │
        └── Steps  (children implementing IPanelStep, activated in hierarchy top-to-bottom order)
              ├── AnimatedStep     — plays an animation clip; optional variant dialogue text
              ├── MiniGame         — abstract; subclass for each puzzle (e.g. SignalGame)
              └── FocusPoint       — STUB; will write a FocusOption to PlayerChoicesSO (see AGENTS.md)

─────────────────────────────────────────
IPANELSTEP CONTRACT
─────────────────────────────────────────

IPanelStep
  │     bool IsBlocking         — if true, Advance() locks input after Activate() until OnStepComplete fires
  │     bool ShowInFinalState   — if true, ShowInstant() calls Activate(); otherwise calls Deactivate()
  │     UnityEvent OnStepComplete
  │     void Activate(PlayerChoicesSO choices)
  │     void Deactivate()
  │     void PrepareForReplay()

ShowInFinalState MUST combine designer intent with runtime state:
  AnimatedStep:  ShowInFinalState => persistsInFinalState && _hasBeenActivated
  MiniGame:      ShowInFinalState => false  (puzzles never persist in history view)

The _hasBeenActivated guard is NOT optional. Calling Activate() on a step that has never been
through Advance() plays its animation outside the blocking system, permanently locking the
advance button because UnblockPanel is never registered as a listener.

─────────────────────────────────────────
COMMANDS
─────────────────────────────────────────

ICommand
  │     Execute()
  │     Undo()
  └── SwitchCameraCommand  (plain C# — implements ICommand)
        │     IComicPanel PanelAfterExecute   (the target panel)
        │     IComicPanel PanelAfterUndo      (the previous panel; null on first launch)
        │     CinemachineBrain _brain
        │     CinemachineBlendDefinition _blend
        │
        │     Execute()  ──►  set brain.DefaultBlend = _blend; prev.Hide(); target.Show()
        │     Undo()     ──►  set brain.DefaultBlend = prev.IncomingBlend; target.Hide(); prev.ShowInstant()
        │     Redo()     ──►  set brain.DefaultBlend = target.IncomingBlend; prev.Hide(); target.ShowInstant()
        │
        └── Execute() calls Show() — story-forward with animation.
            Undo() and Redo() both call ShowInstant() — history navigation never replays animations.

