─────────────────────────────────────────
KEY DESIGN DECISIONS
─────────────────────────────────────────

• PlayerChoicesSO decouples all systems — no class needs a ComicManager reference
  just to know what the player chose. All panels share one asset via [SerializeField].

• PanelDataSO lets non-programmers add/configure panels entirely in the Inspector.
  Name assets Panel_01_, Panel_02_ … so Project window sort = comic order.

• lastLoop on PanelDataSO (default Loop3) retires panels without any code change —
  set it lower on the asset to stop a panel appearing after a specific loop.
  Panel eligibility logic lives solely in PanelSelector.

• List<IComicPanel> replaces Dictionary — rank lives on PanelDataSO, no duplication.

• FocusOption enum (single) replaces three parallel enums — one type, three axes.

• CommandHistory (two stacks) replaces CommandQueue — correct structure for undo/redo.
  Undo/Redo use ShowInstant(); Execute uses Show() — history never replays animations.

• IComicPanel hides Unity types — interface uses Show()/Hide()/UnityEvent, testable
  without Cinemachine/Animator dependencies.

• IPanelStep ShowInFinalState puts both guards (designer flag + runtime activated) inside
  the implementor — ShowInstant() asks one question, gets one answer.

• HasBeenVisited set at end of WaitForIntroCompletion() — navigating away mid-animation
  leaves HasBeenVisited false so the animation replays correctly on the next visit.

• [RequireComponent(typeof(Animator))] on ComicPanel — Animator is always co-located on
  the same GameObject, so it is resolved via GetComponent in Awake rather than [SerializeField].
  Prevents accidental removal and eliminates one manual wiring step per variant.

• NavigationController unblocks input ONLY via OnPanelReadyForInput — the prior
  OnCameraActivated (Cinemachine blend complete) approach caused a race condition where
  the blend could finish before the panel's intro animation, unlocking input prematurely.

• InputAction.performed callback replaces Update() polling in NavigationController.

