SCENE SETUP FOR A PANEL
─────────────────────────────────────────

IMPORTANT — Animator placement rule:
  An Animator can only animate objects within its own GameObject's subtree (itself + descendants).
  The panel Animator MUST be on the ComicPanel ROOT so it can reach all children.
  If the Animator is on a child, it cannot animate siblings, parents, or the root.

ComicPanel_XX_Name (GameObject)          ← ComicPanel.cs + Animator live HERE (root)
  ├── CinemachineCamera                  ← one per panel; starts disabled automatically
  ├── Step_01_Reveal                     ← AnimatedStep (first spacebar press)
  ├── Step_02_Dialogue                   ← AnimatedStep with Label assigned (second press)
  ├── Step_03_SpriteIn                   ← AnimatedStep, purely visual (third press)
  └── Step_04_Puzzle                     ← MiniGame subclass (fourth press — blocks until complete)

Steps activate in hierarchy top-to-bottom order. Reorder by dragging GameObjects in the Hierarchy.
CinemachineCamera starts disabled by Awake(); ComicManager.Start() enables the first panel via Show().

