ORDER OF STEPS IN A PANEL
─────────────────────────────────────────

Spacebar presses proceed 1 → 2 → 3 → 4. Reorder steps by dragging GameObjects in the Hierarchy.

ComicPanel_02_Lab          ← ComicPanel.cs + Animator live here
  ├── Step_01_PanelReveal  ← Step 1 — AnimatedStep (panel slides/fades in)
  ├── Step_02_Dialogue_A   ← Step 2 — AnimatedStep with Label (first caption)
  ├── Step_03_SpriteReveal ← Step 3 — AnimatedStep, visual reveal
  ├── Step_04_Dialogue_B   ← Step 4 — AnimatedStep with Label (second caption)
  └── Step_05_Puzzle       ← Step 5 — MiniGame subclass

─────────────────────────────────────────
SET UP AN ANIMATED STEP
─────────────────────────────────────────

1. Add a child GameObject to the ComicPanel root.
2. Add an Animator component to that child.
3. Create an animation clip; set it as the Animator's default state; disable Loop Time.
4. On the last keyframe, add an Animation Event → Function: OnAnimationFinished
5. Add an AnimatedStep component to the child.

Optional dialogue text: assign a TMP_Text to the Label field. Fill in variant text fields
to show different dialogue based on the player's focus choices.

Persists In Final State: tick this on any AnimatedStep that should remain visible when the
player browses history (UI arrows). Only steps already triggered via Advance() will show —
steps not yet reached are always hidden regardless of this setting (ShowInFinalState guard).

